## Day 02 - Resource Workload and Planning

##1. Objective
The purpose of Day 2 is to prepare a task-level resource plan for the four software projects. The plan allocates six developers (DEV-1 to DEV-6) and two QA engineers (QA-1 and QA-2), each available for up to 8 hours per working day.
The plan identifies resource ownership, weekly capacity, project dependencies, priority order, and possible bottlenecks.

##2. Planning Assumptions
The assessment provides project completion percentages and key concerns, but it does not provide detailed task estimates, named skills, leave schedules, or exact milestone dates. Therefore:
- One planning week is treated as 5 working days.
- Each developer and QA engineer has a maximum capacity of 8 hours per day and 40 hours per week.
- The allocations below are proposed planning hours, not verified remaining-effort estimates.
- Work is assigned according to the project concerns in the assessment.
- Developers are assumed to have the skills needed for their assigned work; the project lead must validate this before confirming assignments.
- The allocation uses all stated capacity for planning purposes. Meetings, support work, leave, and unplanned work must be considered before the plan is baselined.
- No exact delivery forecast is made because milestone dates and task estimates have not been supplied.

##3. Weekly Capacity Calculation
Formula: Weekly capacity = Number of resources × 8 hours per day × 5 working days

Resource group	Number of people	 Hours per person per week	 Total weekly capacity
Developers	            6	                  40                    	240 hours
QA Engineers	          2	                  40	                      80 hours
Total	                  8	                  40	                    320 hours


Daily portfolio capacity is 48 developer hours (6 × 8) and 16 QA hours (2 × 8), giving 64 combined resource hours per working day.

